{"skill":{"slug":"figma","displayName":"Figma"},"version":{"version":"2.1.0","createdAt":1769380900543,"changelog":"Enhanced Figma design analysis and export tools with comprehensive documentation","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6817,"sha256":"c35f45d9ff33561d1cb6bede85ba73b1a825639cbbe3d835d33d12660e42cc5a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"assets/templates/brand-guidelines-template.json","size":1738,"sha256":"bee509bba8666761efd94b875a8564c444274a209d256370c0b62ac1d60cdfbb","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"references/accessibility-guidelines.md","size":12850,"sha256":"2b42060ac1d508608e0690964e54f85b264fa252c5ca3f79c6aaf26444caf2fa","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/design-patterns.md","size":10108,"sha256":"29a878af22781b1d9f992cac1c575aaf48177b376d0ba70afd2f428d5b2ffd1d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/export-formats.md","size":11163,"sha256":"43fae29e8d7ea16acf295a47dfa47bbef35db381b11c96891db2d25e148142d8","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/figma-api-reference.md","size":7256,"sha256":"9edc0d6741af8066d1a0de52b8ff27ceffa3c4b1c0d55c363cb4cd62a4c9801e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":39,"sha256":"9b4e65f5ec3c043848c901e7e46e7a1bf480cc5042f1866c4a20bd7468be7844","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/accessibility_checker.py","size":22014,"sha256":"5c0c2a43462a7ffeb16d2c32d77e757e22834b9243f99ac37da47e57bc91bc42","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/export_manager.py","size":22132,"sha256":"b9510f830d10844a2e8cee97cacdc62811b7f93f72d1795506097efeb76994cc","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/figma_client.py","size":12360,"sha256":"e034e92891ef0b3afe5bd45cd313758cd94c21084121a03e7aa3b86a3d850c73","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/style_auditor.py","size":30444,"sha256":"89d2ca1ed92ec771a6433d8acf0739983133c2eccd9ebc885811d5e7540c0d88","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2873,"sha256":"d861554619612755add7a583bd9feac040789127a309e5f19fea608cca02f621","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789018634278,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"7622d5a56b4987d278d76fc3663fbeb6b776417cdbbe1d531423472a8bfa5232","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/7622d5a56b4987d278d76fc3663fbeb6b776417cdbbe1d531423472a8bfa5232","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: figma\nVersion: 2.1.0\n\nThe OpenClaw AgentSkills skill bundle for Figma is benign. All Python scripts (`figma_client.py`, `export_manager.py`, `accessibility_checker.py`, `style_auditor.py`) are focused on interacting with the Figma API for read-only operations like data extraction, asset export, and design auditing, as explicitly stated in `SKILL.md`. Authentication is handled securely via `FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN` environment variable. Network calls are exclusively directed to `api.figma.com` or Figma's CDN, and file system operations are limited to writing exported assets and reports to user-specified directories, with filename sanitization in place. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence mechanisms, obfuscation, or prompt injection attempts in the `SKILL.md` or any other files.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159972044},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":39,"checkedAt":1789018634278},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is broadly a real Figma analysis/export tool, but its generated HTML reports can include unescaped Figma content that may run active browser content when opened.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to api.figma.com, a Figma token, and local file writes are proportionate for this purpose, but generated HTML reports and caller-controlled output paths lack containment safeguards.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No postinstall script, service, hook, or hidden installer was found. The requirements use lower-bound dependency constraints and include unnecessary or unused packages such as pathlib and aiohttp.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions disclose Figma token use and report/export commands, but they do not warn that collaboratively controlled Figma names and text are inserted into generated HTML reports without escaping.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No persistence mechanism, privilege escalation, background worker, scheduled task, or modification of Figma files was found; writes are limited to user-invoked exports, reports, manifests, and output files.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The Figma API access, asset export, accessibility checks, style audits, and local report generation fit the stated purpose. Some advertised capabilities are overstated or partial, including WEBP export in the documentation and placeholder design-token extraction.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use a least-privileged Figma token from a secret store or environment variable, avoid the --token argument, run exports into a dedicated directory, and treat generated HTML reports as unsafe unless the Figma file and its collaborators are trusted. Prefer pinned dependencies in an isolated environment.","findings":"[TP4] unexpected: The artifact implements substantial Figma functionality, but some claims exceed the code, such as WEBP support in SKILL.md while the CLI allows png, svg, and pdf, and token extraction that returns placeholder values.\n[PE3] expected: A Figma access token is expected for this integration. Reading FIGMA_ACCESS_TOKEN is purpose-aligned, but users should avoid passing tokens through --token or storing them casually in .env files.\n[LP3] expected: The required environment access, network calls, and file writes match the export and reporting purpose, but the skill would benefit from a clearer permissions and output-scope section.\n[SDI-1] expected: Local writes are expected for exports and reports despite the read-only Figma-file claim; the wording should clarify that read-only refers to Figma files, not the local filesystem.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The design-token extraction helpers advertise extraction but use placeholder or fixed values, which is a reliability and disclosure issue rather than evidence of malicious behavior.\n[E1] expected: The observed external endpoint is the documented Figma API or Figma-provided image URLs, which is necessary for the stated functionality.\n[SQP-2] expected: Downloading exported images is expected, but the implementation writes to caller-selected paths without overwrite protection, path restriction, size checks, or content validation.\n[T09] unexpected: The stored HTML injection findings are supported by the code: style and accessibility reports interpolate Figma file and node metadata into HTML without escaping or a restrictive content security policy.\n[T08] unexpected: No malicious dependency was established, but the dependency file is not reproducibly pinned and includes avoidable packages, increasing supply-chain exposure.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789018634278}}}}}